Title: -XdumpFUIR crashes with IndexOutOfBoundsException on Call to a removed field (accessedClazz returns NO_CLAZZ)

Reproducer

fz -XdumpFUIR -e 'say (7.as_i64)'

Observed

java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException: Index -1 out of bounds for length 5539
  at dev.flang.fuir.GeneratingFUIR.id2clazz(GeneratingFUIR.java:739)
  at dev.flang.fuir.GeneratingFUIR.clazzOuterClazz(GeneratingFUIR.java:1077)
  at dev.flang.fuir.FUIR.clazzNameWithArgsAndResult(FUIR.java:212)
  at dev.flang.fuir.FUIR.codeAtAsString(FUIR.java:1159)
  at dev.flang.fuir.FUIR.dumpCode(...)

Root cause

In FUIR.codeAtAsString, the Call branch builds its label via:

java
case Call -> ... clazzNameWithArgsAndResult(accessedClazz(s)) ...

GeneratingFUIR.accessedClazz(s) legitimately returns NO_CLAZZ when the accessed field has been removed (see the res instanceof Clazz rc ? rc._id : NO_CLAZZ return at GeneratingFUIR.java:2431, and the note on assignedType at ~2551).

clazzNameWithArgsAndResult has precondition cl >= firstClazz() and does not tolerate NO_CLAZZ. Since PRECONDITIONS is disabled in the build, -1 is not caught and propagates to clazzOuterClazz(-1) → id2clazz(-1) → IndexOutOfBoundsException.

The parallel Assign branch does not crash because it uses clazzName(accessedClazz(s)), and clazzName tolerates NO_CLAZZ (prints -- no clazz --). The Call branch lacks the equivalent guard.

Impact: dump-only. The program compiles and runs correctly without -XdumpFUIR.

Proposed fix (either):

Guard the Call branch in codeAtAsString for accessedClazz(s) == NO_CLAZZ, mirroring Assign.
Make clazzNameWithArgsAndResult tolerate NO_CLAZZ (return clazzName(cl) early), fixing all callers.